// Cross-engine agreement for discounted reward properties (see .args: -ex, -s, -h, -m).
//
// Undiscounted, [risky] can enter the inescapable positive-reward loop at s=2, so the
// maximiser's total reward is infinite:

// RESULT: Infinity
R{"r"}max=?[C]

// RESULT: 101.0
R{"r"}min=?[C]

// Discounted, every value is finite - which is the whole point of this fixture. A
// symbolic implementation that keeps the usual Prob0/Prob1 (or zero-reward end
// component) precomputation reports Infinity here instead, because that precomputation
// reasons about the undiscounted reachability structure.

// RESULT: 101.0
R{"r"}max=?[C{discount=0.9}]

// RESULT: [24.4995,24.5001]
R{"r"}min=?[C{discount=0.9}]

// The same, as a reachability reward: s=3 is the only reward-free absorbing state, so
// these agree with the total-reward values above.

// RESULT: 101.0
R{"r"}max=?[F{discount=0.9} "target"]

// RESULT: [24.4995,24.5001]
R{"r"}min=?[F{discount=0.9} "target"]

// Bounded cumulative reward, where no precomputation is involved at all - this checks
// the discount reaches the iteration itself.

// RESULT: 3.875
R{"r"}min=?[C{discount=0.5}<=3]

// Discount factor 0: no future value contributes, so this is just the immediate
// expected reward (state reward 1 at s=0, plus the cheaper action's reward 1).

// RESULT: 2.0
R{"r"}min=?[C{discount=0}]

// RESULT: 101.0
R{"r"}max=?[C{discount=0}]

// Discount factor 1 must be identical to no discounting at all.

// RESULT: 101.0
R{"r"}min=?[C{discount=1}]
